Description: install, run and update OSINT command line tools by name
 otinstaller manages open-source OSINT command line tools. It installs each
 tool from a pinned, tested version into its own Python virtualenv under
 ~/.otinstaller, runs it by name, turns typed inputs such as u:johndoe or
 d:example.com into the tool's own flags, and saves every run's output with a
 timestamp and a SHA-256 sidecar.
 .
 It covers about 50 tools for usernames, email addresses, phone numbers,
 domains and URLs, and can run all installed tools that take one kind of
 input at once. Nothing is installed system-wide and no root is needed.
 .
 The tools themselves are downloaded from PyPI and GitHub when you install
 them. Crash reports are off unless the user turns them on.
